      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T12:25:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If there\u0027s no symbols needed to be added except one, why list all of them?",
      "revId": "6fb0dcbbedae0448bf125485021cba5ca910e75f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d055c212_29619d06",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1978086
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T13:05:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The rationale was that in this manner if you were to remove one of the other GKI file lists that were responsible for exporting the symbols we need then the symbols in our file list would keep them exported.\n\nIf you tell us that you will never remove any files / symbols from the GKI file lists once they are there then we are happy to update our patch to just include the one symbol that is actually being added.\n\nWe are still learning the correct procedures for submitting things to GKI and Android in general so please do let us know what is expected / correct way to do things so we can try to get it right first time.",
      "parentUuid": "84124063_e4f394ab",
      "revId": "6fb0dcbbedae0448bf125485021cba5ca910e75f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf2f073d_cac82950",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T17:10:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Listing all of them is the normal process for device oems/vendors. This case is a little different in the sense that the symbols probably should be just those that are required for the filesystem module from tuxera (not sure if it is or not). I don\u0027t see any reason to trim it down since it is only adding the one symbol to the KMI.",
      "parentUuid": "d055c212_29619d06",
      "revId": "6fb0dcbbedae0448bf125485021cba5ca910e75f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ff31482_bfbd1052",
        "filename": "android/abi_gki_aarch64_tuxera",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T12:25:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "no filesystem should be needing this hook, why is this required?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "6fb0dcbbedae0448bf125485021cba5ca910e75f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db3aa2c7_89c0c9fd",
        "filename": "android/abi_gki_aarch64_tuxera",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1978086
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T13:02:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This symbol was approved in our similar GKI patch for android13-5.15 so why not approve it here, too?  Please see: https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/2325113\n\nBut to answer your question: we do not use this symbol at all or at least not knowingly.  It must be pulled in via something that is getting inlined by the compiler.  Perhaps something in a kernel header file that is marked static inline or a sequence of multiple static inline calls.\n\nGiven you asked we will try to figure out where it is coming from - we have never looked before but it can be non-trivial to find...",
      "parentUuid": "1ff31482_bfbd1052",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "6fb0dcbbedae0448bf125485021cba5ca910e75f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ece5e15c_bb31ddeb",
        "filename": "android/abi_gki_aarch64_tuxera",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T17:10:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not a vendor hook, it\u0027s a wrapper function for a hook to allow the hook to be invoked from `static inline void percpu_down_read()`. This must be the first case of `percpu_down_read()` being called from a vendor module, but it doesn\u0027t seem unreasonable to do so.",
      "parentUuid": "db3aa2c7_89c0c9fd",
      "range": {
